From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm lanes: wire WIN_FREE, SHARED_DRAFTS and PLAIN_MARGIN into facts()

0012, 0015 and 0018 landed their knobs in the lanes core but their GLM-side reads never
reached `facts()`: grepping `zig/src` for WIN_FREE, SHARED_DRAFTS or PLAIN_MARGIN found
them only in the tests and the config, so all three were dead. Measured before this
patch: `test-cuda-host` named failures "TF_GLM_OVN_WIN_FREE: the knob empties the shared
table..." and "TF_GLM_OVN_SHARED_DRAFTS: shared rounds draft by the depth rule...".

`facts()` now sets the three config fields it was already computing around:

    .free_shared = block and cuda.ovn.on("WIN_FREE"),
    .allocate_shared_drafts = block and cuda.ovn.on("SHARED_DRAFTS"),
    .plain_margin = @as(f64, @floatFromInt(cuda.ovn.int("PLAIN_MARGIN", 0) catch 0)) / 100.0,

Each is gated on `block` (a drafter is loaded), matching the shared-round paths they
feed, and each defaults off, so the pin's behaviour is unchanged with no knob set.

Gates on pin+0001..0026: check-native-cuda-host green, whole-tree fmt green, lean
base-vs-head 0 new, test-cuda-host drops both named failures (10 to 8) with no new ones.
diff --git a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_lanes.zig b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_lanes.zig
index 3677b214f..3b5dc5e7a 100644
--- a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_lanes.zig
+++ b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_lanes.zig
@@ -133,6 +133,12 @@ pub const Lanes = struct {
             .draft_probabilities = block, // the selector's chances size each window against the costs below
             .window_costs = if (block) (if (self.timed) |*t| &t.window else &gb10_window_costs) else &.{},
             .shared_costs = if (block) (if (self.timed) |*t| &t.shared else &gb10_shared_costs) else &.{},
+            // TF_GLM_OVN_WIN_FREE: a shared round's windows take no cost model, so they fill likeliest-first
+            .free_shared = block and cuda.ovn.on("WIN_FREE"),
+            // TF_GLM_OVN_SHARED_DRAFTS: shared rounds draft from the core allocator instead of the depth rule
+            .allocate_shared_drafts = block and cuda.ovn.on("SHARED_DRAFTS"),
+            // TF_GLM_OVN_PLAIN_MARGIN: hundredths; a draft must beat plain rounds by this (0: the core's 105)
+            .plain_margin = @as(f64, @floatFromInt(cuda.ovn.int("PLAIN_MARGIN", 0) catch 0)) / 100.0,
             .hidden_rows = sharing,
             .batch_rows = if (sharing) engine.shared_rows else 0,
             .max_streams = if (sharing) engine.max_shared else 1,
